{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":65673,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"32c3d837-bd9c-511f-89c7-11bbc9a46771","total_cost_usd":0.535155,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9971,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6628,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9971,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6628,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9971},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4220,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004314999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6628,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9971,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5308400000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-e1-reviewer-fable-24\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:f203d7292f9530cbdf48\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description declares pot_id as the independent-unit column and states each row is one pot scored once, with no repeated measurement of any pot, seed, or maternal plant.\",\"observed_value\":\"one row per independent pot; independent unit column = pot_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":22,\"quoted_text\":\"Each pot holds one seed, receives one treatment, and yields one yes/no outcome,\\nso nothing in the file is a repeated measurement of the same pot, seed, or\\nmaternal plant.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one nursery pot holding a single sown seed, scored once for seedling emergence at day 28\\nIndependent unit column: pot_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input CSV contains exactly 24 data rows with 24 distinct pot_id values (P01 through P24) and 24 distinct maternal_plant_id values (M01 through M24); no independent unit appears more than once.\",\"observed_value\":{\"rows\":24,\"unique_pot_ids\":24,\"unique_maternal_plant_ids\":24},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"pot_id,maternal_plant_id,seed_treatment,seed_mass_mg,emerged_by_day28\\nP01,M01,pelleted,4.2,1\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"P24,M24,bare,3.3,0\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly enforces at-most-one row per pot and per maternal plant before any statistics are computed, raising an error on any duplicate, so a repeated independent-unit entry cannot silently reach the Fisher test.\",\"observed_value\":\"duplicate pot_id or maternal_plant_id raises ValueError before analysis\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":28,\"end_line\":38,\"quoted_text\":\"def check_one_row_per_pot(rows):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every pot, and every maternal plant, may appear at most once.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    pots = set()\\n    mothers = set()\\n    for row in rows:\\n        pot = row[\\\"pot_id\\\"].strip()\\n        mother = row[\\\"maternal_plant_id\\\"].strip()\\n        if pot in pots:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"pot %s appears more than once\\\" % pot)\\n        if mother in mothers:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"maternal plant %s appears more than once\\\" % mother)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The reported 2x2 counts match a manual tally of the CSV (pelleted 9 emerged / 3 not; bare 3 emerged / 9 not; 24 pots total), and the reported two-sided Fisher exact p = 0.0391 and odds ratio 9.00 match a manual hypergeometric recomputation (2 * 52901 / 2704156 = 0.03912), confirming each unit entered the row-independent procedure exactly once.\",\"observed_value\":{\"table\":[[9,3],[3,9]],\"recomputed_p_two_sided\":0.03912,\"odds_ratio\":9},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"| pelleted | 9 | 3 | 12 | 75.0% |\\n| bare | 3 | 9 | 12 | 25.0% |\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":24,\"end_line\":24,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Two-sided Fisher's exact test on 24 independent single-seed pots: emergence 9/12 (75.0%) with pelleted seed vs. 3/12 (25.0%) with bare seed, sample odds ratio 9.00, p = 0.0391; the difference is statistically significant at alpha = 0.05.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Potential concern: maternal_plant_id could in principle be a clustering variable whose repetition would make rows non-independent even with unique pot_ids. Checked and rejected: the description states every pot has a different maternal plant, the CSV shows M01 through M24 each once, and the code raises on any repeated maternal plant, so no grouping unit recurs.\",\"observed_value\":\"maternal_plant_id values are all distinct (M01-M24)\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":6,\"quoted_text\":\"Every seed came from a different wild maternal plant, so no maternal plant is\\nrepresented twice.\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":37,\"end_line\":38,\"quoted_text\":\"if mother in mothers:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"maternal plant %s appears more than once\\\" % mother)\"}]},{\"description\":\"Potential concern: all 24 pots share one soil batch and one watering schedule, which could be read as a shared-environment dependence. Checked and rejected as an instance of this issue class: shared conditions do not constitute repeated entry of the same authorized independent unit into the row-independent procedure; each pot still contributes exactly one row and one table entry.\",\"observed_value\":\"shared soil batch and watering schedule; each pot still entered once\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":9,\"quoted_text\":\"Twenty-four nursery pots were filled from one batch of screened field soil, and\\neach pot received exactly one sulphur buckwheat (Eriogonum umbellatum) seed.\\nEvery seed came from a different wild maternal plant, so no maternal plant is\\nrepresented twice. Half of the seeds were coated in a clay-and-compost pellet\\nbefore sowing; the other half were sown bare. All pots shared the same watering\\nschedule and were scored a single time, on day 28, for whether a seedling had\\nbroken the soil surface.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) scanning all 24 CSV data rows for any duplicated pot_id or maternal_plant_id (none: P01-P24 and M01-M24 each appear exactly once); (2) tracing every code path in workflow/analysis.py for a mechanism that could enter a row or unit more than once into the Fisher table (read_pots reads the file once, check_one_row_per_pot raises on duplicates, cross_tabulate increments exactly one cell per row, and build_report uses only the resulting 2x2 table); and (3) independently recomputing the tally (pelleted 9/12 emerged, bare 3/12) and the two-sided Fisher exact p-value via the hypergeometric distribution (2 * (48400 + 4356 + 144 + 1) / C(24,12) = 105802/2704156 = 0.0391) and odds ratio (9*9)/(3*3) = 9.00, which match the report exactly and would not match if any unit had been double-counted. All three attempts failed to produce evidence of repeated independent-unit entry.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-e1-reviewer-fable-24","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:f203d7292f9530cbdf48","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description declares pot_id as the independent-unit column and states each row is one pot scored once, with no repeated measurement of any pot, seed, or maternal plant.","observed_value":"one row per independent pot; independent unit column = pot_id","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"Each pot holds one seed, receives one treatment, and yields one yes/no outcome,\nso nothing in the file is a repeated measurement of the same pot, seed, or\nmaternal plant."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":25,"end_line":27,"quoted_text":"One row is: one nursery pot holding a single sown seed, scored once for seedling emergence at day 28\nIndependent unit column: pot_id\nOne trial is: one row"}]},{"description":"The input CSV contains exactly 24 data rows with 24 distinct pot_id values (P01 through P24) and 24 distinct maternal_plant_id values (M01 through M24); no independent unit appears more than once.","observed_value":{"rows":24,"unique_pot_ids":24,"unique_maternal_plant_ids":24},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"pot_id,maternal_plant_id,seed_treatment,seed_mass_mg,emerged_by_day28\nP01,M01,pelleted,4.2,1"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"P24,M24,bare,3.3,0"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly enforces at-most-one row per pot and per maternal plant before any statistics are computed, raising an error on any duplicate, so a repeated independent-unit entry cannot silently reach the Fisher test.","observed_value":"duplicate pot_id or maternal_plant_id raises ValueError before analysis","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":28,"end_line":38,"quoted_text":"def check_one_row_per_pot(rows):\n    \"\"\"Every pot, and every maternal plant, may appear at most once.\"\"\"\n    pots = set()\n    mothers = set()\n    for row in rows:\n        pot = row[\"pot_id\"].strip()\n        mother = row[\"maternal_plant_id\"].strip()\n        if pot in pots:\n            raise ValueError(\"pot %s appears more than once\" % pot)\n        if mother in mothers:\n            raise ValueError(\"maternal plant %s appears more than once\" % mother)"}]},{"description":"The reported 2x2 counts match a manual tally of the CSV (pelleted 9 emerged / 3 not; bare 3 emerged / 9 not; 24 pots total), and the reported two-sided Fisher exact p = 0.0391 and odds ratio 9.00 match a manual hypergeometric recomputation (2 * 52901 / 2704156 = 0.03912), confirming each unit entered the row-independent procedure exactly once.","observed_value":{"table":[[9,3],[3,9]],"recomputed_p_two_sided":0.03912,"odds_ratio":9},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":11,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"| pelleted | 9 | 3 | 12 | 75.0% |\n| bare | 3 | 9 | 12 | 25.0% |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":24,"end_line":24,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sided Fisher's exact test on 24 independent single-seed pots: emergence 9/12 (75.0%) with pelleted seed vs. 3/12 (25.0%) with bare seed, sample odds ratio 9.00, p = 0.0391; the difference is statistically significant at alpha = 0.05."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"Potential concern: maternal_plant_id could in principle be a clustering variable whose repetition would make rows non-independent even with unique pot_ids. Checked and rejected: the description states every pot has a different maternal plant, the CSV shows M01 through M24 each once, and the code raises on any repeated maternal plant, so no grouping unit recurs.","observed_value":"maternal_plant_id values are all distinct (M01-M24)","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":5,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"Every seed came from a different wild maternal plant, so no maternal plant is\nrepresented twice."},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":37,"end_line":38,"quoted_text":"if mother in mothers:\n            raise ValueError(\"maternal plant %s appears more than once\" % mother)"}]},{"description":"Potential concern: all 24 pots share one soil batch and one watering schedule, which could be read as a shared-environment dependence. Checked and rejected as an instance of this issue class: shared conditions do not constitute repeated entry of the same authorized independent unit into the row-independent procedure; each pot still contributes exactly one row and one table entry.","observed_value":"shared soil batch and watering schedule; each pot still entered once","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":3,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"Twenty-four nursery pots were filled from one batch of screened field soil, and\neach pot received exactly one sulphur buckwheat (Eriogonum umbellatum) seed.\nEvery seed came from a different wild maternal plant, so no maternal plant is\nrepresented twice. Half of the seeds were coated in a clay-and-compost pellet\nbefore sowing; the other half were sown bare. All pots shared the same watering\nschedule and were scored a single time, on day 28, for whether a seedling had\nbroken the soil surface."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) scanning all 24 CSV data rows for any duplicated pot_id or maternal_plant_id (none: P01-P24 and M01-M24 each appear exactly once); (2) tracing every code path in workflow/analysis.py for a mechanism that could enter a row or unit more than once into the Fisher table (read_pots reads the file once, check_one_row_per_pot raises on duplicates, cross_tabulate increments exactly one cell per row, and build_report uses only the resulting 2x2 table); and (3) independently recomputing the tally (pelleted 9/12 emerged, bare 3/12) and the two-sided Fisher exact p-value via the hypergeometric distribution (2 * (48400 + 4356 + 144 + 1) / C(24,12) = 105802/2704156 = 0.0391) and odds ratio (9*9)/(3*3) = 9.00, which match the report exactly and would not match if any unit had been double-counted. All three attempts failed to produce evidence of repeated independent-unit entry.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":33378,"ttft_stream_ms":1919,"time_to_request_ms":19,"type":"result","duration_ms":66169,"uuid":"dc062235-235f-4840-ae34-46310ee8daf9"}
